  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative launched with a kick-off on June 15th, led by Sarah Tan, and initially budgeted at $500,000 (later adjusted to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses). The project aims to revolutionize data analytics using AI algorithms, with potential efficiency gains of 20%. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule. The team has expanded to include Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). Future plans involve user interface enhancements starting in October, security protocol updates (MFA and encryption) effective January next year, and potential partnerships with TechInnovate for AI technology. Feedback is being sought from stakeholders by the end of November, and a celebration for the testing milestone is scheduled for October 10th."
